From 8d95dc1baf702060757f8b5a87c67247d753ec42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LHBUSA <sales@localhomebuyersusa.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:31:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] /round-by-round read model, rights-first images, CSS
 token drift

Read architecture
- supabase/migrations/20260910150000_ufc_round_index.sql (NOT APPLIED):
  view ufc_round_index (one row per eligible bout, security_invoker,
  service_role only) and rpc ufc_round_index_page() returning totals,
  provenance and five shelves of <= 12 as one jsonb value.
- web/lib/roundIndex.ts: one request instead of ~67 paged table reads. The
  response is validated against its contract; anything short of it throws
  RoundIndexUnavailable. The old pager returned a partial prefix on failure
  and rendered it as the whole archive. Coverage lookups read the view by id,
  <= 60 per request, one row per bout.
- Semantics: the five-round shelf is scheduled_rounds = 5 (a five-round main
  event that ended in R2 is a five-round fight); the stat bar says "rounds
  observed". Archive provenance (round rows, newest capture, build time) is
  printed on the page.
- lib/roundIndex.test.mjs: 8 tests, including one request per page and
  failure on 504 / transport error / truncated JSON / short shelf.

Images
- Removed the ESPN headshot fallback (db.ts, media.ts, next.config.ts
  remotePatterns). A fighter without a stored image cleared for commercial use
  gets no photograph; reads also require commercial_use_allowed. ESPN athlete
  ids stay for identity linkage.
- /about#images now states what production does, including that card
  thumbnails carry no credit line and that official video posters are served
  by YouTube.

Design tokens
- --fs-xs/--fs-md/--fs-lg were referenced 24 times and defined nowhere; they
  now alias the canonical PBE scale by role (sm, body, h3).
- tuf.css season-21 standings named --line/--card/--gold/--muted, which
  nothing defines; mapped to --pbe-* tokens.
- scripts/check-css-tokens.mjs: undefined tokens 7 on main, 0 here.

