Subject: [PATCH 4/4] reconcile: deterministic dry-run planner and guarded SQL
 renderer for duplicate fighter/bout pairs

plan_duplicate_merges.py (GET only) derives, per ESPN bout, the duplicate
UFC Stats-keyed bout and fighter from data, enumerates every reference from
the live schema (all FK columns, uuid[] fighter arrays; jsonb snapshots left
alone), classifies the duplicate fighter's other bouts as twins (must be in
the plan) or unique (repoint only; cannot collide), checks uniqueness
collisions, compares the ESPN and UFC Stats result rows, and emits ordered
operations plus full before-images. Canonical rule: ESPN-keyed rows survive.

render_merge_sql.py turns an eligible plan into ONE transaction: audit rows
first (ufc_identity_reconciliations, migration 20260910170000, NOT applied),
then bout merges, then each fighter merge once; every pair opens with a DO
block that raises on any drift from the plan. It executes nothing.

Dry run 2026-09-10 against production: 8 of 9 pairs eligible; Wiklacz blocked
by a portrait on both rows (human decision). Nothing applied.

